    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Familial adenomatous polyposis",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<strong>A</strong>&nbsp;Gastric foveolar&ndash;type adenoma. The vast majority of gastric adenomas in familial adenomatous polyposis are foveolar-type adenomas with low-grade dysplasia, mainly located in the gastric body; distinction between a fundic gland polyp with low-grade dysplasia and a gastric foveolar&ndash;type adenoma can be difficult, but this is of little importance because the risk of neoplastic progression is very low for both lesions.",
